<title>BULGARIA: Yield falls further on Bulgaria 4-wk T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls further on Bulgaria 4-wk T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yield fell further on Bulgaria's Finance Ministry four-week discount T-bills at the daily auction on Tuesday as the issue was oversubscribed, central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>The average yield to maturity on the issue dropped to 2.93 percent from 3.19 percent at Monday's auction and 3.35 percent on Friday.</p>
<p>The issue was offered with no minimum acceptable price set in advance.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Prices in percent of par:</p>
<p>Issue number		  BG3038297001</p>
<p> Maturity			four weeks</p>
<p> Par value		     18,000 million levs</p>
<p> Issue date		    June 11</p>
<p> Maturity date		 July 9</p>
<p> Bids received		 61,319.9 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	   97.10 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		 18,000 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	  97.15 pct</p>
<p> Avg yield to maturity     2.93 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 91188</p>
